      "id": 1,
      "text": "Peach Bottom began as a ferry crossing, later gaining a railroad station after the Columbia and Port Deposit line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_Bottom%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original town and its station were submerged when the Conowingo Dam was built in 1926‑28.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_Bottom%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The present village sits just southeast of the submerged station site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_Bottom%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Across the river, the Peach Bottom Nuclear Generating Station occupies the original town's site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
